I must confess that I've been following this patch since I like the
concept, but I thought that the "songcasting" system seemed way too
bulky and complicated.  I like your idea for these song effects much
better.  Would using one of these abilities drain mana just like
casting a spell?  Would a bard character know them all, or learn some
of them as he increases in level?  If the former, would there be a
chance of failure for the more powerful effects while the bard is
still low-level?  Finally, would the type of instrument and whether or
not it's magical play into the success rate?

Personally, I the bard knowing all of his powers, but having 100%
failure rates for many of them until he gets higher-level, and his
chance of success being influenced by the type and quality of the
instrument (e.g. magical instruments increase chance of success;
pacify works better with a harp, panic with drums, etc.).  Also, there
should be some chance of success even without an instrument, but a
hefty penalty should be applied, in this case.

Finally, I think a bard should still be able to learn real spells from
spellbooks, but his ability would be similar to one of the weaker
spellcasting classes so that he doesn't become overpowered.

